From 0277345d1b626382f8bcdc0dac51c84128f4eb44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 22:12:46 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] PlaitOS: the LocalSend button hands over files LocalSend can
 read

LocalSend's share handler (share_handler) maps a storage document address
(com.android.externalstorage.documents/document/primary:...) to a path in its own folder,
finds nothing and drops the share (it opened on Receive). Any other content address it copies
through a stream. So the button passes read-only stand-ins from PlaitShareProvider
(not exported, read grant per document, served from the document), as FX's FileProvider
addresses work.

Share intents also take Android's documented ACTION_SEND shape: the file only in
EXTRA_STREAM, no data (as FX sends); the LocalSend button opens it in its own task.

Checked on the phone: one file and two files open on LocalSend's Send screen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017VXjYUWzBqMCeUoJD2Suc4
